    "b-wsum-d1": {
      "id": "b-wsum-d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the summarizer narrates; it does not judge. Outcomes, scores, and sequence numbers come from the checkpoint digest, and the narrative may only explain them. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the legacy condense door let the model restate outcomes and the ledger filled with claims no checkpoint supported. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": this agent, renarration, and any future run-close summary."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-wsum-d2": {
      "id": "b-wsum-d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the summary lane is opt-in per run through --worker-summary. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the seam is new and its cost is one model call per closed worker; the operator turns it on for a run deliberately. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the run loop's start-up wiring."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
